# Character movement
@scenario tutorial_lesson_08
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide point]
pip: A move command changes a character's position over time. Watch Pip move toward the window.
[if !tutorial_still]
[move pip guide stride-a-right exprdur=0]
[move pip window ease_in_out_cubic 740]
[wait 180]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 180]
[move pip window stride-c-right exprdur=0]
[wait 180]
[move pip window stride-b-right exprdur=0]
[wait 200]
[move pip window neutral exprdur=90]
[endif]
[if tutorial_still]
[show pip guide point]
pip: In reduced motion, Pip points toward the window from the starting position.
[else]
pip: Pip is at the second position. The background stayed still.
[endif]
[if !tutorial_still]
[move pip window stride-a-left exprdur=0]
[move pip guide ease_out_cubic 560]
[wait 140]
[move pip guide stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip guide stride-c-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip guide stride-b-left exprdur=0]
[wait 140]
[move pip guide point exprdur=90]
[endif]
pip: Change the duration of the first move, then replay it.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: What lets an actor move without replacing the set?
> A new stage preset. -> retry
> A character position. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: Character positions belong to the actor. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: Character positions belong to the actor.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_08]
[flag tutorial_done_08]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
